#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""unified-review: a panel of models from different labs reviews a draft, then
votes on every finding. For one Markdown file, a local review page opens with
the draft and each finding in place, where Accept writes a change into the
file. unified.md gives the findings by severity, then in draft order, each with
its votes. An optional web fact-check runs in the background and writes
factcheck.md. A PDF or Word file is reviewed as a Markdown copy, and
Download on the page gives the edited copy back in the file's own format.

Usage: unified-review [-o OUTDIR] [-n FOCUS] [-p PANEL] [--context FILE]... [--verify] [--rules FILE] FILE [FILE...]
       unified-review --page FILE                  open the review page for a file
       unified-review --upload                     open a page to upload a file and read its review
       unified-review --item 3,7,K2 [--run DIR]   print items to act on
       unified-review --ignore 5,7 [--note WHY]    record declined findings
       unified-review --applied 3                  record applied findings
       unified-review --unignore D2                lift a past decline
       unified-review --decisions                  list decisions for this folder
       unified-review --forget FILE                start FILE's history over (kept in runs/forgotten)
       unified-review --snapshot FILE              save FILE as FILE-v<N> beside it
       unified-review --changes N FILE             write every change since version N
  -o OUTDIR  where to write output (default: <project>-<file>-v<N> under
             ~/.local/share/unified-review/runs, or $UNIFIED_REVIEW_RUNS)
  -n FOCUS   extra instructions appended to the reviewer prompt
  --context FILE  supporting material the panel reads but does not review
             (reviewer comments, a call, a source paper). Text or PDF. Repeatable.
  -p PANEL   comma-separated panel (default: claude,gpt,gemini). Short names
             claude, gpt, gemini, grok, or harness:model[@effort], such as
             claude:opus or codex:gpt-5.6-luna@medium or cursor:kimi-k3-low
  --verify   also fact-check the draft's claims with web search (background)
  --no-md    review a PDF as is, instead of converting it to Markdown first

Foreground:
  1. review   each panelist reviews the draft, no web search
  2. vote     each panelist votes on every finding, reviewers anonymized
  3. merge    this script groups duplicates, sets aside findings most voters
              reject, runs mechanical checks, writes unified.md, and opens the
              review page (one Markdown file) or unified.md.
Background (only with --verify; detached, started first):
  4. claims   the first panelist lists the draft's checkable claims
  5. verify   each panelist checks every claim with web search, using
              stronger models than the review (FACTCHECK_PANELISTS)
  6. merge    this script keeps the most cautious verdict per claim, writes
              factcheck.md in draft order, and opens it

Env overrides: CLAUDE_BIN, CODEX_BIN, CURSOR_BIN, CLAUDE_MD, UNIFIED_REVIEW_RULES,
UNIFIED_REVIEW_TIMEOUT (seconds per model call), UNIFIED_REVIEW_OPEN_APP
(app that opens the results, default: the default .md app), UNIFIED_REVIEW_PORT
(fixed port for the review page, default: any free port)
"""
import argparse
import collections
import contextlib
import copy
import difflib
import fcntl
import hashlib
import io
import json
import math
import os
import random
import re
import secrets
